1
00:00:00,805 --> 00:00:02,344
(Today, the King of Living Alone)

2
00:00:02,345 --> 00:00:03,445
"The King of Living Alone."

3
00:00:10,585 --> 00:00:11,844
(Gyeong Hye is busy going somewhere in the morning.)

4
00:00:11,845 --> 00:00:13,815
You're keeping busy in the morning.

5
00:00:13,885 --> 00:00:16,454
Right. Whoever walks that fast is bound to be diligent.

6
00:00:16,455 --> 00:00:17,485
Right.

7
00:00:19,955 --> 00:00:20,955
Hello.

8
00:00:20,956 --> 00:00:24,665
I've already been living alone for half a year now.

9
00:00:24,795 --> 00:00:26,264
I'm actor Park Gyeong Hye. Nice to see you again.

10
00:00:26,265 --> 00:00:27,465
She's so cheerful.

11
00:00:29,205 --> 00:00:31,534
(She's living in a tiny 19.8m² studio.)

12
00:00:31,535 --> 00:00:32,735
It's been a while.

13
00:00:33,505 --> 00:00:36,805
(She was a newbie at living alone who moved out 4 months ago.)

14
00:00:38,205 --> 00:00:39,545
(I'll take your order up here.)

15
00:00:40,975 --> 00:00:42,784
(She's a part-timer at night.)

16
00:00:42,785 --> 00:00:43,915
That's the cool cafe.

17
00:00:45,485 --> 00:00:46,984
(She's so cute. This is the reality of living alone.)

18
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:48,354
(I love seeing how hardworking she is.)

19
00:00:48,355 --> 00:00:50,524
Actually, after sharing my day-to-day life...

20
00:00:50,525 --> 00:00:52,555
in this studio on the show,

21
00:00:52,755 --> 00:00:53,924
so many people expressed...

22
00:00:53,925 --> 00:00:55,054
- their support for me. - Right.

23
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:59,595
Hye Soo, Tae Hyun, In Na,

24
00:00:59,865 --> 00:01:02,405
and other seniors whom I worked with...

25
00:01:02,605 --> 00:01:05,105
called and texted me to express their support.

26
00:01:05,275 --> 00:01:08,305
When I ran into people on the streets,

27
00:01:08,475 --> 00:01:11,574
so many of them wished me good luck for my solo life.

28
00:01:11,575 --> 00:01:14,144
That's why I'm more willing to do things on my own...

29
00:01:14,145 --> 00:01:16,615
even if I end up making mistakes and redoing them.

30
00:01:16,745 --> 00:01:18,445
That's been my attitude.

31
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:20,755
So there are more things I can handle on my own now.

32
00:01:20,885 --> 00:01:22,825
That's what I can tell you about myself now.

33
00:01:24,485 --> 00:01:27,694
Actually, I passed by the cafe you worked at to see you.

34
00:01:27,695 --> 00:01:29,024
- Really? - But you weren't there.

35
00:01:29,025 --> 00:01:30,294
- I did too. - You too?

36
00:01:30,295 --> 00:01:32,065
- Really? - I always check when I pass by.

37
00:01:32,335 --> 00:01:34,334
So many people came to the cafe to show their support.

38
00:01:34,335 --> 00:01:37,304
I've received so many letters as well.

39
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:38,874
I see. A lot of people expressed their support.

40
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:40,374
- People came to show their support. - I see.

41
00:01:40,375 --> 00:01:44,245
Yes. I wanted to thank everyone who came to show their support.

42
00:01:47,575 --> 00:01:50,285
(While carrying a big shopping bag, )

43
00:01:52,715 --> 00:01:54,014
(she's going somewhere alone.)

44
00:01:54,015 --> 00:01:55,155
Where is she going?

45
00:01:59,295 --> 00:02:00,595
Aren't you her?

46
00:02:01,555 --> 00:02:02,895
- The actress? - I am.

47
00:02:03,395 --> 00:02:05,225
- You are? - She recognized you right away.

48
00:02:05,595 --> 00:02:07,464
- She's shy. She whispered. - Thank you.

49
00:02:07,465 --> 00:02:08,535
I remember you.

50
00:02:08,665 --> 00:02:09,765
You look beautiful.

51
00:02:10,905 --> 00:02:11,965
Thank you.

52
00:02:12,135 --> 00:02:13,434
- Bye. - Bye.

53
00:02:13,435 --> 00:02:14,604
Bye.

54
00:02:14,605 --> 00:02:16,445
(Chuckling)

55
00:02:18,245 --> 00:02:19,275
What a proud moment.

56
00:02:21,345 --> 00:02:23,044
People love it when they see you on the streets, right?

57
00:02:23,045 --> 00:02:24,685
- Yes. I'm grateful for that. - Right.

58
00:02:24,915 --> 00:02:26,414
The moment you're recognized as an actress,

59
00:02:26,415 --> 00:02:27,915
you become a national star.

60
00:02:29,985 --> 00:02:30,985
That's nice.

61
00:02:30,986 --> 00:02:33,995
(She's happily heading somewhere.)

62
00:02:35,825 --> 00:02:39,164
(She has arrived...)

63
00:02:39,165 --> 00:02:43,235
(at a community service center?)

64
00:02:44,905 --> 00:02:46,035
Hello.

65
00:02:49,705 --> 00:02:53,345
(She stops in front of a huge machine upon entering.)

66
00:02:58,145 --> 00:02:59,825
Where did you go with the plastic bottles?

67
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,285
(She grabs a plastic bottle.)

68
00:03:02,325 --> 00:03:04,685
(Inserting)

69
00:03:05,925 --> 00:03:07,894
(She keeps on putting them into the machine.)

70
00:03:07,895 --> 00:03:08,965
What's she doing?

71
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,195
You can trade in the bottles there.

72
00:03:12,335 --> 00:03:15,294
You just have to remove the label sheets around the bottles.

73
00:03:15,295 --> 00:03:16,365
(That's right.)

74
00:03:18,205 --> 00:03:19,635
What will she get in return?

75
00:03:20,605 --> 00:03:23,045
Actually, I didn't know about this when I went here before.

76
00:03:23,305 --> 00:03:26,215
Then I noticed this huge machine one day.

77
00:03:26,315 --> 00:03:28,051
I wondered what it was and asked them about it.

78
00:03:28,075 --> 00:03:31,145
When I put in the plastic bottles, they give me points in return.

79
00:03:31,315 --> 00:03:34,484
And they said I could use the points like cash.

80
00:03:34,485 --> 00:03:36,154
- Really? - So I got interested.

81
00:03:36,155 --> 00:03:38,794
Let me explain. We're bound to use plastic bottles...

82
00:03:38,795 --> 00:03:40,524
when we're filming.

83
00:03:40,525 --> 00:03:44,095
So I suddenly remembered all the plastic bottles on set.

84
00:03:44,695 --> 00:03:45,935
I was like, "That's all money."

85
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,295
Did you take all of them with you?

86
00:03:48,365 --> 00:03:50,234
After finding out about the machine,

87
00:03:50,235 --> 00:03:52,374
I shared this information on set.

88
00:03:52,375 --> 00:03:53,604
Everyone drinks water...

89
00:03:53,605 --> 00:03:54,834
- from plastic bottles on set. - Yes.

90
00:03:54,835 --> 00:03:57,874
They said, "Do you want to take them, Gyeong Hye?"

91
00:03:57,875 --> 00:03:59,074
So I've been taking a lot of them.

92
00:03:59,075 --> 00:04:01,244
(She's collecting a lot of plastic bottles thanks to them.)

93
00:04:01,245 --> 00:04:03,284
I'll drink up the water and give it to you.

94
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:05,714
- Thank you so much. - I'll drink three bottles today.

95
00:04:05,715 --> 00:04:07,414
- Seriously. Today? - You can take them.

96
00:04:07,415 --> 00:04:08,984
- That's great. - I'll drink three bottles of it.

97
00:04:08,985 --> 00:04:09,985
It's a promise.

98
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:13,694
There are so many benefits from the community service centers.

99
00:04:13,695 --> 00:04:15,594
- They also offer a lot of classes. - Yes.

100
00:04:15,595 --> 00:04:17,601
- Educational programs. - Yes. They offer such programs.

101
00:04:17,625 --> 00:04:18,795
In the centers?

102
00:04:18,895 --> 00:04:21,134
Do you work at the center? How come you know everything?

103
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:22,804
My community service center is nearby.

104
00:04:22,805 --> 00:04:24,564
- I borrowed tools from the center. - Right.

105
00:04:24,565 --> 00:04:26,674
You didn't pass the civil service exam, right?

106
00:04:26,675 --> 00:04:28,334
(He continues to suspect Dae Ho.)

107
00:04:28,335 --> 00:04:30,474
I've been feeling insecure about my career lately.

108
00:04:30,475 --> 00:04:33,474
(I've been feeling insecure about my career lately.)

109
00:04:33,475 --> 00:04:34,674
I've been insecure. So I'm going to work hard.

110
00:04:34,675 --> 00:04:37,045
You know everything civil servants would know.

111
00:04:37,285 --> 00:04:40,385
You see so many interesting programs when you look around the center.

112
00:04:40,515 --> 00:04:41,855
You seem like a different person.

113
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:45,155
(Popping it into the machine)

114
00:04:46,095 --> 00:04:48,455
- I see. One by one? - Yes. It's like a vending machine.

115
00:04:49,765 --> 00:04:52,334
They give me 100 points per bottle.

116
00:04:52,335 --> 00:04:53,464
That's one cent.

117
00:04:53,465 --> 00:04:54,835
One cent?

118
00:04:56,305 --> 00:04:59,035
(She keeps on putting in the bottles.)

119
00:05:05,075 --> 00:05:06,214
(Points earned: 2,900 points)

120
00:05:06,215 --> 00:05:07,875
- Did you already hit the limit? - Right.

121
00:05:07,975 --> 00:05:09,575
I found out for the first time that day.

122
00:05:09,945 --> 00:05:12,184
I could only bring in 30 bottles a day...

123
00:05:12,185 --> 00:05:13,361
- It can't go over 30? - because...

124
00:05:13,385 --> 00:05:14,815
To keep anyone from hogging it.

125
00:05:15,825 --> 00:05:17,324
- That's true. - To make sure no one hogs it.

126
00:05:17,325 --> 00:05:19,794
- If persistent people try this, - Right.

127
00:05:19,795 --> 00:05:21,024
They could make 600,000 dollars.

128
00:05:21,025 --> 00:05:22,565
- Right. - That's so true. People...

129
00:05:23,065 --> 00:05:24,594
- If this becomes their thing... - It's not even about the money.

130
00:05:24,595 --> 00:05:26,235
- They'll be there all day long. - Right.

131
00:05:28,265 --> 00:05:30,405
That's 3,000 points.

132
00:05:31,405 --> 00:05:32,534
(She saved 3,000 points today.)

133
00:05:32,535 --> 00:05:34,175
- You accumulated quite a lot. - Yes.

134
00:05:34,505 --> 00:05:36,375
- Right. - She has 4,540 points.

135
00:05:37,075 --> 00:05:38,804
You can use these points to buy a lot of things.

136
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:41,775
Gosh, I need double the points.

137
00:05:42,945 --> 00:05:45,584
The thing is, I shop at Daiso a lot.

138
00:05:45,585 --> 00:05:49,354
I thought it'd feel great to use the points at Daiso.

139
00:05:49,355 --> 00:05:51,124
- I earned these points. - Right.

140
00:05:51,125 --> 00:05:52,795
I was happy when I found out...

141
00:05:53,155 --> 00:05:54,525
I could use the points there.

142
00:05:56,425 --> 00:05:57,764
(After checking her points...)

143
00:05:57,765 --> 00:05:59,435
Gosh, I learned a new thing from her.

144
00:06:01,995 --> 00:06:04,405
I'd go there often if I lived close to the center.

145
00:06:06,275 --> 00:06:09,405
(Instead of heading home, Gyeong Hye gets in the car.)

146
00:06:10,345 --> 00:06:11,445
- What? - My gosh.

147
00:06:11,745 --> 00:06:14,645
Where is she going now? She's super busy.

148
00:06:15,815 --> 00:06:16,985
(You said)

149
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:19,255
(I was the only one you loved)

150
00:06:19,985 --> 00:06:22,885
(Swaying)

151
00:06:24,525 --> 00:06:27,795
(Suddenly getting sad)

152
00:06:28,495 --> 00:06:31,165
(She nails every genre of music in the car.)

153
00:06:32,025 --> 00:06:33,834
(She's driving somewhere in a good mood.)

154
00:06:33,835 --> 00:06:35,875
Wait. That's the way to the cafe where you work at.

155
00:06:36,465 --> 00:06:39,135
- She must be going there to work. - To work?

156
00:06:40,035 --> 00:06:41,374
(Humming)

157
00:06:41,375 --> 00:06:42,905
Look at her, carrying all that stuff.

158
00:06:44,045 --> 00:06:46,375
(Is she making haste to get to work?)

159
00:06:48,475 --> 00:06:50,414
(Chuckling)

160
00:06:50,415 --> 00:06:52,485
(Laughing)

161
00:06:53,585 --> 00:06:56,855
- Right. That's the cafe. - She's going there to work.

162
00:06:57,385 --> 00:06:59,055
- Yes. That's the cafe. What? - What?

163
00:07:01,295 --> 00:07:05,495
(Staring)

164
00:07:05,995 --> 00:07:06,995
(A construction site?)

165
00:07:06,996 --> 00:07:09,534
The cafe closed down.

166
00:07:09,535 --> 00:07:12,305
- The cafe closed down. - Really?

167
00:07:12,475 --> 00:07:13,675
The cafe wasn't there anymore.

168
00:07:14,075 --> 00:07:17,745
(She worked at the cafe while building her acting career.)

169
00:07:18,675 --> 00:07:22,114
(She had worked there for 2 years.)

170
00:07:22,115 --> 00:07:23,355
- That was a hip cafe. - Enjoy.

171
00:07:23,645 --> 00:07:26,054
Wait. My old favorite spot is gone now?

172
00:07:26,055 --> 00:07:27,735
Right. You have memories about this place.

173
00:07:29,325 --> 00:07:31,985
(Her lovely place of work for the past 2 years...)

174
00:07:32,085 --> 00:07:33,194
(is under renovation.)

175
00:07:33,195 --> 00:07:34,301
- Why all of a sudden? - What?

176
00:07:34,325 --> 00:07:35,665
Why did it close down?

177
00:07:35,765 --> 00:07:39,595
The thing is, the owner of the cafe...

178
00:07:39,695 --> 00:07:42,534
gave birth to this beautiful baby.

179
00:07:42,535 --> 00:07:45,465
As a new parent, she wouldn't be able to...

180
00:07:45,535 --> 00:07:49,605
manage the cafe like she used to, realistically speaking.

181
00:07:49,775 --> 00:07:52,845
So we all worked together on its last day, May 12.

182
00:07:53,475 --> 00:07:56,015
Then I said goodbye to the cafe.

183
00:07:58,515 --> 00:08:01,715
(Gyeong Hye recorded her last day at the cafe.)

184
00:08:02,655 --> 00:08:04,785
(She spent 2 years working at this cafe.)

185
00:08:06,255 --> 00:08:07,824
I always drank there.

186
00:08:07,825 --> 00:08:09,825
- Right. The window seat, right? - Yes, that's it.

187
00:08:11,265 --> 00:08:12,265
(Extracting the last cup of coffee before closing)

188
00:08:12,266 --> 00:08:15,295
I was extracting coffee on my last day.

189
00:08:15,435 --> 00:08:17,905
I teared up a bit too.

190
00:08:19,175 --> 00:08:20,934
That must feel weird.

191
00:08:20,935 --> 00:08:22,895
- Their last shift? - Yes, it's their last shift.

192
00:08:23,345 --> 00:08:25,045
It's so sad because...

193
00:08:27,075 --> 00:08:28,345
Why am I choking up?

194
00:08:30,245 --> 00:08:31,314
You worked there for two years.

195
00:08:31,315 --> 00:08:32,755
- That must feel weird. - Of course.

196
00:08:33,285 --> 00:08:35,154
Working at the cafe was one thing. But I had gotten close...

197
00:08:35,155 --> 00:08:37,224
- to the other workers. - You have a lot of memories.

198
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:39,994
Right. I was so used to seeing them at work.

199
00:08:39,995 --> 00:08:41,254
The thought of not being able to...

200
00:08:41,255 --> 00:08:42,525
- see them again... - Right.

201
00:08:42,625 --> 00:08:44,125
- made me sad. - Yes.

202
00:08:44,465 --> 00:08:46,705
I picked the worst day to go back to the cafe because...

203
00:08:46,835 --> 00:08:48,995
There used to be a sign.

204
00:08:49,065 --> 00:08:52,265
But they switched the doors for the new business that day.

205
00:08:52,435 --> 00:08:54,604
- It's sadder. - Right. I guess...

206
00:08:54,605 --> 00:08:56,575
that made me feel more emotional.

207
00:08:57,805 --> 00:09:00,415
(A lot has changed already.)

208
00:09:01,115 --> 00:09:02,214
(Her former place of work changed a lot.)

209
00:09:02,215 --> 00:09:03,685
I'm sad about the news too.

210
00:09:04,645 --> 00:09:08,415
(She can't seem to walk away from the cafe.)

211
00:09:11,185 --> 00:09:13,525
(Sighing)

212
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:17,124
- Hello, sir. - Hello.

213
00:09:17,125 --> 00:09:18,425
It's been a while.

214
00:09:18,665 --> 00:09:20,765
Hello. Oh, hi, there.

215
00:09:21,035 --> 00:09:24,904
Actually, the restaurant owner made great meals and snacks for us.

216
00:09:24,905 --> 00:09:26,404
He runs a taco restaurant.

217
00:09:26,405 --> 00:09:27,974
I dropped by to give him some rice cakes...

218
00:09:27,975 --> 00:09:31,075
and have a delicious taco as an early lunch.

219
00:09:31,305 --> 00:09:34,114
I also wanted to say goodbye one last time.

220
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:37,445
Actually, I went there to tell him I'd stop by often.

221
00:09:39,815 --> 00:09:40,985
I'm about to tear up.

222
00:09:42,855 --> 00:09:44,524
This is the first time I saw the construction work.

223
00:09:44,525 --> 00:09:45,955
- Really? - The cafe... Yes.

224
00:09:46,825 --> 00:09:48,455
"This is my new place of work."

225
00:09:50,465 --> 00:09:52,145
She's going to steal the part-timer's job.

226
00:09:52,365 --> 00:09:53,934
- I won't leave the restaurant. - Right.

227
00:09:53,935 --> 00:09:56,604
That's the most familiar spot if there's any.

228
00:09:56,605 --> 00:09:57,905
- My gosh. - Right.

229
00:09:58,505 --> 00:10:00,934
Oh, right. This is nothing big.

230
00:10:00,935 --> 00:10:02,474
You can have them with your staff.

231
00:10:02,475 --> 00:10:04,004
- Really? - I brought rice cakes and sikhye.

232
00:10:04,005 --> 00:10:07,015
- Really? - They're really tasty.

233
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:08,344
I order them for myself too.

234
00:10:08,345 --> 00:10:10,885
- How kind. - She's so good at sharing.

235
00:10:11,215 --> 00:10:12,915
I wanted you to try some too.

236
00:10:13,415 --> 00:10:15,585
- Thank you. We'll enjoy them. - Don't mention it.

237
00:10:16,685 --> 00:10:17,885
Okay.

238
00:10:18,485 --> 00:10:20,725
- That's my order. Thank you. - Sure.

239
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,455
- It won't take long. - Okay.

240
00:10:23,125 --> 00:10:25,694
Doesn't it feel a bit empty with the cafe gone now?

241
00:10:25,695 --> 00:10:28,595
The cafe and our restaurant seemed to make a good team.

242
00:10:28,765 --> 00:10:29,864
- Right. - Your restaurant helped a lot.

243
00:10:29,865 --> 00:10:30,865
Customers came to the cafe...

244
00:10:30,865 --> 00:10:31,865
- after having a meal here. - Right.

245
00:10:31,866 --> 00:10:33,235
So we were grateful too.

246
00:10:33,735 --> 00:10:34,805
We feel the same way.

247
00:10:35,305 --> 00:10:37,004
- You want coffee after the taco. - Yes.

248
00:10:37,005 --> 00:10:38,545
- Right. - They make a good combo.

249
00:10:39,075 --> 00:10:42,245
We had to say goodbye to each other out of the blue.

250
00:10:43,045 --> 00:10:45,284
- Here's your drink. - Thank you.

251
00:10:45,285 --> 00:10:46,355
Sure.

252
00:10:47,185 --> 00:10:49,555
Oh, my. Sir.

253
00:10:50,225 --> 00:10:51,524
Gosh, look at her reaction.

254
00:10:51,525 --> 00:10:52,924
She didn't even look at it.

255
00:10:52,925 --> 00:10:54,855
You can't have guacamole without nachos.

256
00:10:55,095 --> 00:10:57,795
You always take such good care of me when I come here to eat.

257
00:10:57,995 --> 00:10:59,394
- Thank you for the food. - Sure.

258
00:10:59,395 --> 00:11:00,995
- I didn't order that. - Oh, my.

259
00:11:01,235 --> 00:11:02,904
- That looks good. - It was on the house.

260
00:11:02,905 --> 00:11:04,505
- It was on the house. - Thank you.

261
00:11:05,635 --> 00:11:06,774
(Crunchy)

262
00:11:06,775 --> 00:11:08,235
(Humming)

263
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:10,005
I'm in trouble.

264
00:11:11,275 --> 00:11:12,375
This tastes so good.

265
00:11:14,045 --> 00:11:15,045
(Humming)

266
00:11:16,215 --> 00:11:19,085
I love guacamole.

267
00:11:19,285 --> 00:11:20,955
- It's so good. - Yes.

268
00:11:21,285 --> 00:11:22,415
That does look good.

269
00:11:23,225 --> 00:11:26,395
(She takes a big bite of the taco.)

270
00:11:27,655 --> 00:11:30,295
(This is what I'm talking about.)

271
00:11:30,595 --> 00:11:32,425
- It's so good. - Thank you.

272
00:11:32,635 --> 00:11:33,965
Are you still working part-time?

273
00:11:35,265 --> 00:11:38,034
- The cafe closed down. - Right. Are you unemployed now?

274
00:11:38,035 --> 00:11:40,275
(Joking)

275
00:11:40,775 --> 00:11:42,215
You don't need a part-timer, do you?

276
00:11:42,975 --> 00:11:44,175
Give me your resume.

277
00:11:44,475 --> 00:11:45,575
She asked him right away.

278
00:11:45,845 --> 00:11:47,375
I'd have to do an interview, right?

279
00:11:47,575 --> 00:11:48,951
Working at a taco place suits you too.

280
00:11:48,975 --> 00:11:51,684
Are you still looking for a part-time job?

281
00:11:51,685 --> 00:11:53,654
Right now, I'm working on a project with my acting...

282
00:11:53,655 --> 00:11:55,055
- which I'm grateful for. - Right.

283
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:57,855
But I'm worried that...

284
00:11:58,225 --> 00:12:01,794
I feel quite down when I'm not working on any project.

285
00:12:01,795 --> 00:12:04,765
But when I keep working, I get a sense of achievement...

286
00:12:04,895 --> 00:12:07,194
and can feel that I'm using my energy for something.

287
00:12:07,195 --> 00:12:09,435
So when I'm between projects again,

288
00:12:09,605 --> 00:12:10,904
having a part-time job...

289
00:12:10,905 --> 00:12:12,204
- is really helpful. - Right.

290
00:12:12,205 --> 00:12:13,845
- That's great. - It's good to have work.

291
00:12:14,635 --> 00:12:16,344
(Taking a bite while feeling gratitude)

292
00:12:16,345 --> 00:12:18,705
- Seriously. It's so good. - Gosh, she's eating with gusto.

293
00:12:19,575 --> 00:12:22,175
This is nice. You're eating taco, and he's eating the rice cakes.

294
00:12:23,045 --> 00:12:26,555
(The heartwarming scene of sharing food)

295
00:12:26,815 --> 00:12:27,915
This is sad.

296
00:12:29,585 --> 00:12:31,255
I'll come by often to eat here.

297
00:12:31,725 --> 00:12:33,954
- Everyone's sad. - It was nice to see you around.

298
00:12:33,955 --> 00:12:34,955
Right.

299
00:12:35,195 --> 00:12:37,435
We saw each other quite often when I worked at the cafe.

300
00:12:37,495 --> 00:12:41,494
- It feels like I'm a local here. - At first, I didn't recognize you.

301
00:12:41,495 --> 00:12:43,034
- Right. - "She looks familiar."

302
00:12:43,035 --> 00:12:44,364
I see. Really?

303
00:12:44,365 --> 00:12:46,235
Yes. You were wearing overalls then.

304
00:12:47,205 --> 00:12:48,274
Oh, right.

305
00:12:48,275 --> 00:12:49,945
You love making small talk.

306
00:12:50,775 --> 00:12:51,875
She's like an American.

307
00:12:52,175 --> 00:12:53,491
I was like, "I've seen her somewhere."

308
00:12:53,515 --> 00:12:56,685
But to think that I won't see you guys often...

309
00:12:57,385 --> 00:12:58,985
I'll come back to eat here.

310
00:12:59,285 --> 00:13:00,654
The food was great today.

311
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,514
- Bye. Thank you. - Bye.

312
00:13:02,515 --> 00:13:03,624
You didn't take your card.

313
00:13:03,625 --> 00:13:04,625
Thank you.

314
00:13:04,626 --> 00:13:07,155
- She didn't take her card? - She didn't. She must go back.

315
00:13:07,355 --> 00:13:09,764
I forget to take my card so often.

316
00:13:09,765 --> 00:13:12,224
Nowadays, you have to pay at the machine yourself.

317
00:13:12,225 --> 00:13:13,771
- Right. - You know where I had to go back?

318
00:13:13,795 --> 00:13:15,334
I left my card at Mungyeongsaejae Pass...

319
00:13:15,335 --> 00:13:16,435
- on a weekend. - Oh, no!

320
00:13:16,765 --> 00:13:18,204
- I had to go back there. - What?

321
00:13:18,205 --> 00:13:19,265
- Really? - Yes.

322
00:13:19,535 --> 00:13:21,074
- Why didn't you... - You could've gotten it renewed.

323
00:13:21,075 --> 00:13:22,205
Why did you go back?

324
00:13:22,745 --> 00:13:25,345
I could have gotten it renewed.

325
00:13:25,905 --> 00:13:27,375
(I didn't think of that.)

326
00:13:27,745 --> 00:13:29,845
- That sounds so dumb. - Oh, that...

327
00:13:29,945 --> 00:13:31,915
I told you to call me whenever you had problems.

328
00:13:32,185 --> 00:13:33,514
Why are you telling me that now?

329
00:13:33,515 --> 00:13:35,254
When else could I have told you?

330
00:13:35,255 --> 00:13:36,575
(He learned something new today.)

331
00:13:36,755 --> 00:13:38,154
Thank you. Bye.

332
00:13:38,155 --> 00:13:39,355
The food was great!

333
00:13:40,625 --> 00:13:43,194
(This goodbye)

334
00:13:43,195 --> 00:13:46,295
(Won't be forever)

335
00:13:47,135 --> 00:13:50,005
(Leaving behind the sorrow of parting...)

336
00:13:51,035 --> 00:13:52,305
Let's go.

337
00:13:52,775 --> 00:13:54,174
- She came home. - She came home.

338
00:13:54,175 --> 00:13:55,235
- There. - She's home.

339
00:13:58,205 --> 00:14:00,844
- There's no elevator. - Right. There's no elevator.

340
00:14:00,845 --> 00:14:02,075
(We're in the same boat.)

341
00:14:10,155 --> 00:14:11,224
What?

342
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:13,555
- My gosh. It looks much better now. - Gosh.

343
00:14:15,925 --> 00:14:18,295
- Yes. He fixed it up. - Oh, him. Yes.

344
00:14:18,665 --> 00:14:20,135
- Let's try this. - He went viral.

345
00:14:20,835 --> 00:14:22,804
Everyone wanted to know who this handsome guy was.

346
00:14:22,805 --> 00:14:23,934
- Really? - He went viral.

347
00:14:23,935 --> 00:14:25,665
See? It's all about our looks.

348
00:14:25,965 --> 00:14:27,174
Appearance is what matters.

349
00:14:27,175 --> 00:14:29,305
Did you just figure that out? We must work hard.

350
00:14:30,645 --> 00:14:32,404
- He only did that. - If you're handsome, you get...

351
00:14:32,405 --> 00:14:33,874
- famous by putting on stickers. - Of course.

352
00:14:33,875 --> 00:14:34,914
- We won't get 300,000 views... - Hey.

353
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:35,974
Even if we eat the sheets.

354
00:14:35,975 --> 00:14:37,015
- We can't. - Right.

355
00:14:37,145 --> 00:14:38,915
I should run 100km for my marathon.

356
00:14:39,455 --> 00:14:40,455
You should.

357
00:14:41,155 --> 00:14:44,785
(She and Chan Hyeong put the sheets only on the cabinet doors.)

358
00:14:46,355 --> 00:14:48,654
(The whole sink cabinet looks white now.)

359
00:14:48,655 --> 00:14:50,194
It does look much cleaner now.

360
00:14:50,195 --> 00:14:51,995
It changed the vibe of your house completely.

361
00:14:52,165 --> 00:14:53,594
- It looks completely different. - So...

362
00:14:53,595 --> 00:14:55,495
I'm really proud because...

363
00:14:55,735 --> 00:14:57,005
I did the rest by myself.

364
00:14:57,105 --> 00:14:58,634
- Great job. - Really?

365
00:14:58,635 --> 00:15:00,035
- You did a great job. - Right.

366
00:15:00,075 --> 00:15:02,804
Yes. I worked really hard on it. And I did it all by myself.

367
00:15:02,805 --> 00:15:04,444
I was so proud of finishing this job...

368
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,445
- all by myself. - It's a proud moment.

369
00:15:05,446 --> 00:15:07,375
That's why you're the king of living alone now.

370
00:15:07,745 --> 00:15:09,025
You're the king of living alone.

371
00:15:09,245 --> 00:15:10,925
- It looks like a new sink cabinet. - Yes.

372
00:15:11,615 --> 00:15:14,455
(Next to the sink cabinet decorated by the king of living alone...)

373
00:15:17,325 --> 00:15:18,885
- What's going on? - What?

374
00:15:19,855 --> 00:15:21,555
- You still haven't finished it. - What?

375
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:23,424
- I see. But your stuff... - Are you packing?

376
00:15:23,425 --> 00:15:24,625
What's going on? What is this?

377
00:15:25,065 --> 00:15:28,865
(Under the top bunk bed which she set up last time, )

378
00:15:29,505 --> 00:15:31,204
(it's clustered with clothes.)

379
00:15:31,205 --> 00:15:32,634
- I got more stuff as I lived there. - Right.

380
00:15:32,635 --> 00:15:35,575
I started to run out of space to store them.

381
00:15:36,405 --> 00:15:39,275
It turns out I don't have an eye for design.

382
00:15:39,645 --> 00:15:41,415
I have no idea what goes well with what.

383
00:15:41,815 --> 00:15:43,945
I'm not good at matching things up.

384
00:15:44,145 --> 00:15:48,055
So I'm ready for a new challenge to push myself to grow.

385
00:15:49,485 --> 00:15:52,055
(After changing into comfortable clothes...)

386
00:15:52,855 --> 00:15:54,555
(Hopping over)

387
00:15:56,165 --> 00:15:59,995
(She shoves her things into a suitcase as big as her.)

388
00:16:01,295 --> 00:16:04,365
(Adding more things to an already-full suitcase)

389
00:16:05,605 --> 00:16:08,205
(Lugging)

390
00:16:09,505 --> 00:16:11,544
Where is she going now? My gosh.

391
00:16:11,545 --> 00:16:12,575
Where is she going?

392
00:16:12,745 --> 00:16:14,375
- She has so much energy. - Seriously.

393
00:16:14,575 --> 00:16:16,345
Seriously. She has so much stamina.

394
00:16:16,545 --> 00:16:17,914
People like her make good runners.

395
00:16:17,915 --> 00:16:19,415
(Showing interest)

396
00:16:20,785 --> 00:16:22,814
(Shoving the bags into the back seat)

397
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:23,855
All done.

398
00:16:27,155 --> 00:16:28,795
(Opening up)

399
00:16:34,795 --> 00:16:36,034
The moving boxes?

400
00:16:36,035 --> 00:16:38,304
(She takes out moving boxes from the trunk.)

401
00:16:38,305 --> 00:16:39,934
(Glancing back)

402
00:16:39,935 --> 00:16:41,635
Put in the passcode.

403
00:16:42,135 --> 00:16:43,175
Wait.

404
00:16:45,545 --> 00:16:47,344
- Hello, sir. - "Sir?"

405
00:16:47,345 --> 00:16:49,514
- Are you from a furniture company? - Wait.

406
00:16:49,515 --> 00:16:50,814
- Yes. - A furniture company?

407
00:16:50,815 --> 00:16:52,184
Are you from a furniture company?

408
00:16:52,185 --> 00:16:53,255
- Yes. - Hello.

409
00:16:54,015 --> 00:16:55,354
(She bought another piece of furniture after the bunk bed?)

410
00:16:55,355 --> 00:16:57,185
- Where... - Will you sleep standing up?

411
00:16:58,025 --> 00:16:59,795
There's no spare space.

412
00:17:01,725 --> 00:17:04,365
Well, winter is gone, and summer is here.

413
00:17:04,495 --> 00:17:07,234
I don't have a lot of summer clothes here.

414
00:17:07,235 --> 00:17:09,865
I still have some of my clothes at my parents' house...

415
00:17:09,905 --> 00:17:12,805
because I don't have much space here.

416
00:17:13,305 --> 00:17:15,805
I made a big decision of buying a closet.

417
00:17:16,135 --> 00:17:18,475
I can switch my winter clothes for summer clothes.

418
00:17:18,745 --> 00:17:21,814
I'm going to transition my house from winter to summer.

419
00:17:21,815 --> 00:17:24,685
For this new makeover, this is what I've prepared.

420
00:17:25,315 --> 00:17:27,015
Greed is endless when living alone!

421
00:17:27,985 --> 00:17:30,054
It looks like you and I are quite similar.

422
00:17:30,055 --> 00:17:31,484
You keep changing your house.

423
00:17:31,485 --> 00:17:33,095
(Shaking hands)

424
00:17:33,355 --> 00:17:35,625
I bet she'll bring in sand pretty soon.

425
00:17:36,925 --> 00:17:39,635
(The ultimate house of endless desires, Dae Ho's house)

426
00:17:40,335 --> 00:17:41,795
It still feels like a dream.

427
00:17:43,065 --> 00:17:44,665
Right. It wasn't a dream.

428
00:17:45,435 --> 00:17:46,504
Wait. It's not going in.

429
00:17:46,505 --> 00:17:48,905
(She gets ready to bring more changes to the house.)

430
00:17:50,005 --> 00:17:52,705
(I must get rid of them quickly.)

431
00:17:53,345 --> 00:17:55,615
(Pulling down)

432
00:17:56,845 --> 00:17:59,444
(Quickly disassembling the rack)

433
00:17:59,445 --> 00:18:00,455
She's so quick.

434
00:18:02,885 --> 00:18:04,284
(Going up and down the stairs...)

435
00:18:04,285 --> 00:18:05,924
I should slow down.

436
00:18:05,925 --> 00:18:06,925
(nonstop)

437
00:18:06,926 --> 00:18:09,155
Gosh, no. Thank you.

438
00:18:11,925 --> 00:18:13,794
- You're throwing that out. - Right. Throw it out.

439
00:18:13,795 --> 00:18:15,955
(She's throwing out the furniture she no longer uses.)

440
00:18:17,205 --> 00:18:18,664
(Meanwhile, the new furniture is being brought up.)

441
00:18:18,665 --> 00:18:19,834
It's quite big.

442
00:18:19,835 --> 00:18:22,835
(Meanwhile, the new furniture is being brought up.)

443
00:18:24,045 --> 00:18:25,244
(Quickly running up after him)

444
00:18:25,245 --> 00:18:26,814
Times like this make me feel so bad...

445
00:18:26,815 --> 00:18:28,344
that I live in a building without an elevator.

446
00:18:28,345 --> 00:18:29,545
I feel the same way.

447
00:18:30,545 --> 00:18:32,544
(As soon as she comes back, )

448
00:18:32,545 --> 00:18:35,014
(she opens up the fridge.)

449
00:18:35,015 --> 00:18:37,885
- I'm sorry. The AC isn't working. - No, it's okay.

450
00:18:38,455 --> 00:18:40,725
Would you like some sikhye?

451
00:18:41,395 --> 00:18:43,124
It's nothing compared to your help.

452
00:18:43,125 --> 00:18:44,624
- Gosh, how thoughtful of you. - Right. She must offer drinks.

453
00:18:44,625 --> 00:18:46,785
I'm sorry for making you work in this bad environment.

454
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:50,635
(Scanning)

455
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:52,604
Right?

456
00:18:52,605 --> 00:18:53,675
(Crouching down)

457
00:18:54,235 --> 00:18:56,905
(She sits in the corner quietly and observes them.)

458
00:18:57,405 --> 00:19:00,375
(Staring)

459
00:19:01,875 --> 00:19:04,545
(Last time when she set up her bed...)

460
00:19:04,845 --> 00:19:06,454
(You know what I think?)

461
00:19:06,455 --> 00:19:08,654
(I'm living alone for the first time in my life.)

462
00:19:08,655 --> 00:19:09,854
Did you not drink this on purpose?

463
00:19:09,855 --> 00:19:12,225
(She stayed next to him and talked nonstop.)

464
00:19:12,885 --> 00:19:15,955
(Ghost Small Talk had emerged into the studio.)

465
00:19:16,765 --> 00:19:19,835
(I used to install air conditioners for a living before.)

466
00:19:20,995 --> 00:19:22,964
(This kind of customer is the most uncomfortable.)

467
00:19:22,965 --> 00:19:25,805
(Shocked)

468
00:19:26,035 --> 00:19:27,775
(It's nice that you offered him coffee.)

469
00:19:28,075 --> 00:19:30,045
(But I get nervous in case I mess things up.)

470
00:19:31,175 --> 00:19:34,015
You tried to stay out of their sight and stayed quiet.

471
00:19:34,275 --> 00:19:35,415
Look at her hiding there.

472
00:19:36,115 --> 00:19:39,315
(She quietly observes them.)

473
00:19:39,985 --> 00:19:42,454
After hearing that from Ji Hyeon, I started to act more carefully.

474
00:19:42,455 --> 00:19:45,084
I got to hear a different perspective from him.

475
00:19:45,085 --> 00:19:47,025
I mean, he used to be in a similar line of work.

476
00:19:47,125 --> 00:19:48,701
- I realized I missed that. - You could understand his point.

477
00:19:48,725 --> 00:19:51,125
After realizing what I overlooked, I couldn't help...

478
00:19:51,165 --> 00:19:52,464
but be more careful.

479
00:19:52,465 --> 00:19:53,764
Ji Hyeon spared a lot of people the trouble.

480
00:19:53,765 --> 00:19:56,095
(Joking)

481
00:19:56,505 --> 00:19:59,065
(She stays quiet not to bother the workers.)

482
00:19:59,735 --> 00:20:01,734
I want to try that.

483
00:20:01,735 --> 00:20:04,405
She has so many things to say, but her mouth is shut tightly.

484
00:20:05,745 --> 00:20:07,745
- I bet she bit her tongue. - Right.

485
00:20:09,345 --> 00:20:10,385
It's not here.

486
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:15,515
Do you feel uncomfortable that I'm watching you guys?

487
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:19,484
Other customers also watch us work.

488
00:20:19,485 --> 00:20:21,555
- It's nice that we get to... - Yes.

489
00:20:21,955 --> 00:20:24,924
Show you the parts you can't see once we assemble everything...

490
00:20:24,925 --> 00:20:26,594
while we work on this.

491
00:20:26,595 --> 00:20:28,234
- Right. - That's great.

492
00:20:28,235 --> 00:20:29,935
(Lightening up)

493
00:20:30,805 --> 00:20:33,475
As you saw earlier, I used to have a rack here.

494
00:20:33,705 --> 00:20:36,375
- But I love to cook. - Yes.

495
00:20:36,475 --> 00:20:39,944
So my clothes started to smell like food.

496
00:20:39,945 --> 00:20:41,075
I see. Right.

497
00:20:42,015 --> 00:20:43,744
I actually have rhinitis too.

498
00:20:43,745 --> 00:20:45,615
- Me too. - Really?

499
00:20:45,885 --> 00:20:47,855
I know effective medicine for rhinitis.

500
00:20:48,615 --> 00:20:49,754
When I ventilate the house,

501
00:20:49,755 --> 00:20:50,854
- pollen comes in. - Right.

502
00:20:50,855 --> 00:20:52,554
- And it'd stick on my clothes. - Yes.

503
00:20:52,555 --> 00:20:54,495
Then pollen and I get locked up in this house.

504
00:20:55,895 --> 00:20:57,364
- So I needed a closet. - There she goes again.

505
00:20:57,365 --> 00:20:58,471
(Ghost Small Talk is emerging out.)

506
00:20:58,495 --> 00:21:01,435
I just carry a nasal spray with me because it gets frustrating.

507
00:21:01,465 --> 00:21:03,965
And you also have to think about dust.

508
00:21:04,005 --> 00:21:05,365
"I shouldn't have responded."

509
00:21:06,905 --> 00:21:08,575
You have to drill it hard. Right?

510
00:21:08,805 --> 00:21:10,174
You must drill it hard and carefully.

511
00:21:10,175 --> 00:21:11,644
They're talking about drilling too?

512
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:13,251
(Their conversation is flowing smoothly.)

513
00:21:13,275 --> 00:21:15,244
You can call me if you have any questions.

514
00:21:15,245 --> 00:21:16,684
I take calls until 10pm.

515
00:21:16,685 --> 00:21:19,184
You always know the sweetest things to say.

516
00:21:19,185 --> 00:21:20,214
- Me? - Yes.

517
00:21:20,215 --> 00:21:22,784
I need to be kind to my customers.

518
00:21:22,785 --> 00:21:25,085
