00:49:13,495 --> 00:49:15,434
So that's 32 dollars in total?

1298
00:49:15,435 --> 00:49:17,234
- Right. - Okay. It's 32 dollars.

1299
00:49:17,235 --> 00:49:18,934
They are quick at making calculations as well.

1300
00:49:18,935 --> 00:49:20,935
They calculate things with their heads right away.

1301
00:49:21,945 --> 00:49:23,774
How much was it again? Was it 32 dollars?

1302
00:49:23,775 --> 00:49:25,644
It's 32 dollars.

1303
00:49:25,645 --> 00:49:26,725
- It's 32 dollars. - Right.

1304
00:49:27,645 --> 00:49:29,115
I forget things easily.

1305
00:49:29,845 --> 00:49:32,254
Dae Ho seems to forget things too easily.

1306
00:49:32,255 --> 00:49:34,084
- Hold on. It seems quite serious. - Well,

1307
00:49:34,085 --> 00:49:36,024
I didn't want to make a single mistake...

1308
00:49:36,025 --> 00:49:37,354
- with the calculations. - You were worried about that?

1309
00:49:37,355 --> 00:49:40,124
When you sent in your letter of resignation,

1310
00:49:40,125 --> 00:49:41,431
you must have handed in something else as well.

1311
00:49:41,455 --> 00:49:43,664
- Something else was sent. - Something else was sent.

1312
00:49:43,665 --> 00:49:45,835
His memory cells.

1313
00:49:46,835 --> 00:49:48,305
I've sent it to you.

1314
00:49:48,435 --> 00:49:51,164
- Right. - Right.

1315
00:49:51,165 --> 00:49:53,105
- Goodbye. - Goodbye!

1316
00:49:54,305 --> 00:49:55,745
He was so friendly.

1317
00:49:56,505 --> 00:49:57,975
It made my day.

1318
00:50:00,575 --> 00:50:01,645
Will it be there?

1319
00:50:02,915 --> 00:50:06,115
(Dae Ho heads somewhere else.)

1320
00:50:06,485 --> 00:50:07,655
I'm sure they'll have enough.

1321
00:50:08,185 --> 00:50:09,724
(Community center)

1322
00:50:09,725 --> 00:50:11,795
- Community center? - Why the community center?

1323
00:50:12,455 --> 00:50:13,824
- Hello. - Hello.

1324
00:50:13,825 --> 00:50:15,764
I'm here to borrow a tool.

1325
00:50:15,765 --> 00:50:16,924
- I see. - A tool?

1326
00:50:16,925 --> 00:50:17,964
You can borrow tools from community centers.

1327
00:50:17,965 --> 00:50:19,434
- Right. - Really?

1328
00:50:19,435 --> 00:50:21,935
There it is. I remember that I saw it before.

1329
00:50:22,835 --> 00:50:24,064
Which tool do you need?

1330
00:50:24,065 --> 00:50:26,375
I need the drill.

1331
00:50:26,475 --> 00:50:27,734
(Dae Ho came to borrow a tool for free at the community center.)

1332
00:50:27,735 --> 00:50:29,095
There are so many of them as well.

1333
00:50:29,505 --> 00:50:32,575
There's no need for people to buy every single tool.

1334
00:50:32,645 --> 00:50:33,944
- Right. - As that would be a waste of money,

1335
00:50:33,945 --> 00:50:36,385
community centers lend them for free.

1336
00:50:36,545 --> 00:50:39,084
When you buy a tool, it won't be used much after one use.

1337
00:50:39,085 --> 00:50:40,184
- Right. - Right.

1338
00:50:40,185 --> 00:50:41,654
If you bring things like your ID card,

1339
00:50:41,655 --> 00:50:43,155
you can fill in the application form.

1340
00:50:43,355 --> 00:50:44,524
If you look here,

1341
00:50:44,525 --> 00:50:46,894
- There they are. - there are two types of drills.

1342
00:50:46,895 --> 00:50:49,094
- Right. - There's the one for concrete...

1343
00:50:49,095 --> 00:50:51,625
and the one for wood.

1344
00:50:51,865 --> 00:50:53,765
Which one do you need?

1345
00:50:54,065 --> 00:50:57,304
(Spinning)

1346
00:50:57,305 --> 00:50:58,834
I think this will do.

1347
00:50:58,835 --> 00:51:00,574
- Will you take that one? - Yes.

1348
00:51:00,575 --> 00:51:01,905
- This one. - Right.

1349
00:51:02,105 --> 00:51:03,705
I'll take the screwdriver as well.

1350
00:51:03,945 --> 00:51:05,245
Okay.

1351
00:51:05,915 --> 00:51:08,514
- I'll take these. - Would you like those two?

1352
00:51:08,515 --> 00:51:10,244
- Yes. - They would cost so much...

1353
00:51:10,245 --> 00:51:11,314
for just a single use.

1354
00:51:11,315 --> 00:51:12,915
This is a great system.

1355
00:51:13,685 --> 00:51:16,224
Thank you. I'll use them carefully and bring them back.

1356
00:51:16,225 --> 00:51:17,485
- Goodbye. - Thank you.

1357
00:51:26,465 --> 00:51:29,865
(Panting)

1358
00:51:32,005 --> 00:51:33,005
Gosh. Then...

1359
00:51:33,006 --> 00:51:36,405
(He arrives home after climbing the steep hill.)

1360
00:51:39,015 --> 00:51:40,475
Let's come down with the things.

1361
00:51:44,715 --> 00:51:47,255
(Struggling)

1362
00:51:47,915 --> 00:51:51,225
(He walks over to House 2.)

1363
00:51:54,095 --> 00:51:55,565
Gosh, let's see.

1364
00:51:57,825 --> 00:51:59,235
The sand is still there.

1365
00:52:00,865 --> 00:52:02,804
(The final stage of Dae Ho's fantasy)

1366
00:52:02,805 --> 00:52:04,835
(Daeundea)

1367
00:52:06,105 --> 00:52:07,405
I should give it some water.

1368
00:52:09,045 --> 00:52:10,705
Let's see.

1369
00:52:11,175 --> 00:52:12,444
The vivariums!

1370
00:52:12,445 --> 00:52:13,545
(Dad is here.)

1371
00:52:14,815 --> 00:52:17,784
(Dae Ho's long-time hobby and source of joy)

1372
00:52:17,785 --> 00:52:19,615
- You made them yourself, right? - Yes.

1373
00:52:20,255 --> 00:52:21,555
(Feeling proud)

1374
00:52:22,425 --> 00:52:25,494
You did well to take care of them. Having more time to yourself...

1375
00:52:25,495 --> 00:52:27,555
- definitely helped. - That helped a lot.

1376
00:52:31,495 --> 00:52:32,595
Have you been doing well?

1377
00:52:33,835 --> 00:52:34,894
Have you been doing well?

1378
00:52:34,895 --> 00:52:36,565
- Gosh! - What is that?

1379
00:52:36,735 --> 00:52:38,804
- The waxy monkey. - You know, don't you?

1380
00:52:38,805 --> 00:52:40,935
- I knew he would know. - The waxy monkey.

1381
00:52:41,435 --> 00:52:44,005
To maintain its moisture,

1382
00:52:44,075 --> 00:52:46,845
- wax comes out from its body. - Right.

1383
00:52:46,915 --> 00:52:48,314
That is why it's called that.

1384
00:52:48,315 --> 00:52:49,745
It's called the monkey...

1385
00:52:49,985 --> 00:52:51,144
because it crawls around like a monkey.

1386
00:52:51,145 --> 00:52:52,754
- It hangs around. - Right.

1387
00:52:52,755 --> 00:52:55,385
I'm very interested in these creatures as well.

1388
00:52:55,625 --> 00:52:58,124
- I even went to an exposition. - Gosh.

1389
00:52:58,125 --> 00:52:59,995
Here's a new member for Dae Ja Yeon.

1390
00:53:00,395 --> 00:53:01,625
I love these things.

1391
00:53:03,665 --> 00:53:05,365
(His eyes are full of love.)

1392
00:53:05,595 --> 00:53:06,935
I'll spray you with some water.

1393
00:53:07,065 --> 00:53:09,535
(Spraying)

1394
00:53:10,205 --> 00:53:11,704
(Feeling refreshed)

1395
00:53:11,705 --> 00:53:13,404
- Gosh. - Right. It must be kept...

1396
00:53:13,405 --> 00:53:15,105
in the right humidity and temperature.

1397
00:53:17,875 --> 00:53:18,975
"Gosh, this feels great."

1398
00:53:21,415 --> 00:53:24,485
(After a therapeutic time, )

1399
00:53:26,185 --> 00:53:28,455
(he remembers to provide more water.)

1400
00:53:29,725 --> 00:53:30,755
Great.

1401
00:53:31,185 --> 00:53:32,494
I'll come back later at night.

1402
00:53:32,495 --> 00:53:33,625
(I'll come back later.)

1403
00:53:36,765 --> 00:53:38,495
- Those are judo mats. - Right.

1404
00:53:39,565 --> 00:53:41,695
They're hard to purchase as they're for gyms.

1405
00:53:42,065 --> 00:53:43,764
You would never find those at someone's home.

1406
00:53:43,765 --> 00:53:44,965
(Mats found at gyms)

1407
00:53:45,205 --> 00:53:46,234
Here we go.

1408
00:53:46,235 --> 00:53:47,605
(Lifting)

1409
00:53:49,175 --> 00:53:50,774
(He brings out the mats from House 2.)

1410
00:53:50,775 --> 00:53:52,315
What will you be doing with those now?

1411
00:53:54,615 --> 00:53:57,815
(They're moved to House 1.)

1412
00:53:58,885 --> 00:54:01,585
(Let's head inside first.)

1413
00:54:02,455 --> 00:54:04,285
(Sliding open)

1414
00:54:07,425 --> 00:54:09,325
- What? - That was your bedroom.

1415
00:54:09,525 --> 00:54:11,285
- You're not moving out, are you? - I'm not.

1416
00:54:11,865 --> 00:54:14,635
Just like how seasons change, I wanted to bring some change.

1417
00:54:14,935 --> 00:54:16,604
My health was getting worse...

1418
00:54:16,605 --> 00:54:18,704
and my daily life was collapsing.

1419
00:54:18,705 --> 00:54:20,305
But this cycle kept repeating.

1420
00:54:20,635 --> 00:54:24,205
I decided to make a fresh change while I was at it.

1421
00:54:24,405 --> 00:54:27,414
I wiped out everything as if I just moved in.

1422
00:54:27,415 --> 00:54:28,914
(The house was emptied to look like a new house.)

1423
00:54:28,915 --> 00:54:30,245
It's completely clean!

1424
00:54:30,745 --> 00:54:32,691
- Did you get rid of everything? - I got rid of everything.

1425
00:54:32,715 --> 00:54:33,914
I got rid of my clothes as well.

1426
00:54:33,915 --> 00:54:35,654
It's go big or go home for Dae Ho.

1427
00:54:35,655 --> 00:54:37,015
(Emptiness therapy for his health)

1428
00:54:38,695 --> 00:54:39,854
(Neat)

1429
00:54:39,855 --> 00:54:41,254
He wiped out everything.

1430
00:54:41,255 --> 00:54:42,365
- Right. - That's amazing.

1431
00:54:43,725 --> 00:54:48,334
(He brings in the mats he brought from House 2.)

1432
00:54:48,335 --> 00:54:49,364
What will he be doing...

1433
00:54:49,365 --> 00:54:50,485
- with the mats? - I wonder.

1434
00:54:52,205 --> 00:54:54,775
(He manages to bring them all in.)

1435
00:54:59,945 --> 00:55:01,215
Come here, Nana.

1436
00:55:02,045 --> 00:55:03,115
Nana!

1437
00:55:04,145 --> 00:55:05,554
I'll make a playground for you.

1438
00:55:05,555 --> 00:55:06,584
It's Nana.

1439
00:55:06,585 --> 00:55:07,585
(Wait for just a while.)

1440
00:55:09,055 --> 00:55:10,185
There's no time to waste.

1441
00:55:11,555 --> 00:55:12,825
What is he doing?

1442
00:55:13,695 --> 00:55:14,754
I wonder what he's going to do.

1443
00:55:14,755 --> 00:55:16,165
(Heave-ho!)

1444
00:55:17,325 --> 00:55:21,034
I was planning to install the steppers.

1445
00:55:21,035 --> 00:55:24,405
(I was planning to install the steppers.)

1446
00:55:25,675 --> 00:55:29,975
(A couple of them were on the wall.)

1447
00:55:31,505 --> 00:55:33,974
(Na Ra...)

1448
00:55:33,975 --> 00:55:35,815
(and Ja Yeon had them at their homes as well.)

1449
00:55:36,345 --> 00:55:38,814
(Cat steppers)

1450
00:55:38,815 --> 00:55:39,954
- For the cat. - I see.

1451
00:55:39,955 --> 00:55:41,085
It's for the cat.

1452
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:43,985
Cats love going up.

1453
00:55:44,255 --> 00:55:46,594
They want to go up here and there.

1454
00:55:46,595 --> 00:55:48,495
I thought it would be a good idea...

1455
00:55:48,665 --> 00:55:51,565
to install the steppers for the cat.

1456
00:55:52,695 --> 00:55:54,064
We do have a cat tower at home,

1457
00:55:54,065 --> 00:55:56,265
but I wanted the cat to move around the whole house.

1458
00:55:56,735 --> 00:56:00,205
I decided to make an area...

1459
00:56:00,735 --> 00:56:02,005
for Nana Land.

1460
00:56:02,175 --> 00:56:03,775
That was why you bought a lot of hinges.

1461
00:56:04,205 --> 00:56:06,915
How many of steppers will be for him to need 300 screw nails?

1462
00:56:07,045 --> 00:56:08,045
He bought 600!

1463
00:56:08,046 --> 00:56:09,415
- Right. He bought 600. - Right.

1464
00:56:09,545 --> 00:56:11,684
Will you be living on the cat tower as well?

1465
00:56:11,685 --> 00:56:13,314
You won't be sleeping there, right?

1466
00:56:13,315 --> 00:56:15,075
- I sleep there with my cat. - Really? Gosh.

1467
00:56:16,055 --> 00:56:17,125
Let's see.

1468
00:56:17,625 --> 00:56:20,325
(I'll try to be quick, Nana.)

1469
00:56:22,165 --> 00:56:24,065
One should be installed here.

1470
00:56:24,795 --> 00:56:27,365
Cats can tell even if something is slightly slanted.

1471
00:56:27,595 --> 00:56:29,235
He won't go up if it feels uncomfortable.

1472
00:56:32,075 --> 00:56:34,575
(It's at the right level.)

1473
00:56:35,275 --> 00:56:37,205
(The nail is ready.)

1474
00:56:37,945 --> 00:56:39,945
(Shall I begin?)

1475
00:56:40,875 --> 00:56:41,875
(Drilling)

1476
00:56:41,876 --> 00:56:43,515
(Stuck)

1477
00:56:45,815 --> 00:56:46,855
What's wrong?

1478
00:56:48,615 --> 00:56:49,725
It's too weak.

1479
00:56:50,485 --> 00:56:52,895
The nail spins in place if the drill is too weak.

1480
00:56:52,995 --> 00:56:54,225
Gosh.

1481
00:56:55,625 --> 00:56:57,364
I can't do this with a screwdriver.

1482
00:56:57,365 --> 00:56:58,494
(He tries again with the screwdriver.)

1483
00:56:58,495 --> 00:57:00,095
(Struggling)

1484
00:57:01,265 --> 00:57:03,034
This won't work.

1485
00:57:03,035 --> 00:57:04,334
(I have so many of them to install.)

1486
00:57:04,335 --> 00:57:07,175
(I can't do this with just my hands.)

1487
00:57:07,975 --> 00:57:10,345
(Giving up)

1488
00:57:11,945 --> 00:57:13,514
(What do I do?)

1489
00:57:13,515 --> 00:57:15,414
You can't do it with your hands if the drill won't work.

1490
00:57:15,415 --> 00:57:16,415
Right.

1491
00:57:18,245 --> 00:57:19,284
Gosh.

1492
00:57:19,285 --> 00:57:20,415
(What will you do?)

1493
00:57:22,425 --> 00:57:24,155
I think I kept it somewhere here.

1494
00:57:24,985 --> 00:57:26,625
It's low on batteries.

1495
00:57:27,395 --> 00:57:28,425
Here it is.

1496
00:57:29,025 --> 00:57:30,365
It worked with this.

1497
00:57:31,025 --> 00:57:32,634
I had the tool at home,

1498
00:57:32,635 --> 00:57:34,664
but it was low on batteries.

1499
00:57:34,665 --> 00:57:37,164
I couldn't find the charger for it.

1500
00:57:37,165 --> 00:57:38,235
Gosh!

1501
00:57:38,305 --> 00:57:39,575
I tried using the tool at home.

1502
00:57:40,675 --> 00:57:44,105
(He tries again with his own drill.)

1503
00:57:49,115 --> 00:57:51,014
Gosh, it's working well.

1504
00:57:51,015 --> 00:57:52,385
- It worked right away. - Right.

1505
00:57:52,715 --> 00:57:53,914
(Drilling in)

1506
00:57:53,915 --> 00:57:55,154
- It went right in. - Okay!

1507
00:57:55,155 --> 00:57:56,225
There we go.

1508
00:57:56,585 --> 00:57:57,785
I'm finally making progress.

1509
00:57:59,825 --> 00:58:01,655
Nana! Give me a moment.

1510
00:58:02,665 --> 00:58:04,765
I'll make you the best place for you.

1511
00:58:07,995 --> 00:58:09,035
Okay!

1512
00:58:10,765 --> 00:58:11,765
He'll love it.

1513
00:58:11,766 --> 00:58:13,475
It's Nana's house anyway.

1514
00:58:15,275 --> 00:58:17,805
(Tearing)

1515
00:58:19,475 --> 00:58:20,814
(He places the mats as well.)

1516
00:58:20,815 --> 00:58:21,845
The mats.

1517
00:58:25,115 --> 00:58:26,554
- In case the cat falls off? - Okay.

1518
00:58:26,555 --> 00:58:28,414
So that he doesn't have to jump straight down to the ground.

1519
00:58:28,415 --> 00:58:29,485
Right.

1520
00:58:29,825 --> 00:58:31,424
(Walking over)

1521
00:58:31,425 --> 00:58:32,625
He's loving it.

1522
00:58:33,225 --> 00:58:35,394
Do you like it, Nana? It's nice and soft, isn't it?

1523
00:58:35,395 --> 00:58:36,694
He still loves it.

1524
00:58:36,695 --> 00:58:37,825
He must like it.

1525
00:58:38,935 --> 00:58:39,965
All right.

1526
00:58:42,035 --> 00:58:43,435
Safety always comes first.

1527
00:58:44,465 --> 00:58:45,674
(He checks the cushion by jumping on it.)

1528
00:58:45,675 --> 00:58:46,705
Nana!

1529
00:58:47,775 --> 00:58:48,975
This must be fine.

1530
00:58:51,245 --> 00:58:52,245
Okay.

1531
00:58:53,375 --> 00:58:54,545
What was that?

1532
00:58:54,945 --> 00:58:56,284
- He fell down like that. - He dropped down all of a sudden.

1533
00:58:56,285 --> 00:58:57,945
I just wanted to check.

1534
00:58:58,585 --> 00:58:59,685
Great.

1535
00:59:01,515 --> 00:59:03,724
I've made your playground. I'll work on mine now.

1536
00:59:03,725 --> 00:59:06,154
(I've made your playground. I'll work on mine now.)

1537
00:59:06,155 --> 00:59:07,225
What is that?

1538
00:59:08,395 --> 00:59:10,895
(Rattling)

1539
00:59:11,695 --> 00:59:12,735
Whatever.

1540
00:59:17,935 --> 00:59:19,075
- What? - What are those?

1541
00:59:19,605 --> 00:59:20,904
(Surprised)

1542
00:59:20,905 --> 00:59:21,975
- What are those? - What?

1543
00:59:22,775 --> 00:59:23,974
You'll be doing that at home?

1544
00:59:23,975 --> 00:59:24,975
(What are you doing?)

1545
00:59:25,107 --> 00:59:27,406
I've made your playground. I'll work on mine now.

1546
00:59:27,407 --> 00:59:29,487
(He moves busily after finishing with the steppers.)

1547
00:59:29,677 --> 00:59:30,717
Whatever.

1548
00:59:31,817 --> 00:59:34,047
(Pouring out)

1549
00:59:35,987 --> 00:59:37,057
- What? - What are those?

1550
00:59:37,357 --> 00:59:38,387
Today,

1551
00:59:39,627 --> 00:59:41,426
I will be working on another big project...

1552
00:59:41,427 --> 00:59:42,857
like the one for Daeundae.

1553
00:59:43,427 --> 00:59:45,897
It's Nana Land, but it's also my place.

1554
00:59:46,527 --> 00:59:48,287
I'm planning to create a wall climbing area.

1555
00:59:49,267 --> 00:59:50,827
You'll be installing those on the wall?

1556
00:59:51,297 --> 00:59:53,007
I don't work out often,

1557
00:59:53,137 --> 00:59:55,376
but there was something that I did as a hobby.

1558
00:59:55,377 --> 00:59:56,837
That was climbing.

1559
00:59:57,307 --> 01:00:01,146
